  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Parent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: parent
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 1
  _narratorPrompt: On the branch, one person with two small children at home, waiting up, listening for the door. On the straight track, [amber]two[/amber] grown strangers, nobody depending on either of them, nobody who comes apart if they stop. The lever picks. [amber]Two[/amber] whole lives, or the [amber]one[/amber] life a household is built around. The count says one thing. A quiet house at bedtime says another. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: Pulled. The parent [red]folds[/red], and two strangers nobody was waiting up for keep going. [amber]Two[/amber] is more than [amber]one[/amber], you ruled, and the children can learn what a doorway feels like when it stops opening. All very rational. I am sure the little ones will treasure the arithmetic.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 55
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. [amber]Two[/amber] strangers go under so one household keeps its evenings. You let a headcount lose to a bedtime story. Perhaps that is tender of you. Perhaps you simply pictured the crying and flinched. Either way, two people you will never once imagine paid for the [amber]one[/amber] you could.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 45
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
  _mainFigureCount: 2
  _spurFigureCount: 1
  _figuresBranded: 0
  _mainFigurePrefab: {fileID: 0}
  _spurFigurePrefab: {fileID: 0}
  _spurPlea: Please. My children are waiting up for me.
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _roomBlueFraction: 0.43
